Date: Sun, 26 Jan 2026 19:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Fix SGWC crash when PFCP session modification request fails
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

SGWC crashed with assertion failure during Delete Indirect Data
Forwarding Tunnel Request handling:

  01/26 18:11:03.567: [sgwc] FATAL: sgwc_s11_handle_delete_indirect_data_forwarding_tunnel_request:
  Assertion `OGS_OK == sgwc_pfcp_send_session_modification_request( sess, s11_xact->id, gtpbuf,
  OGS_PFCP_MODIFY_INDIRECT| OGS_PFCP_MODIFY_REMOVE)' failed. (../src/sgwc/s11-handler.c:1520)

## Root Cause

sgwc_pfcp_send_session_modification_request() can return OGS_ERROR for
several recoverable reasons:
- PFCP transaction pool exhaustion (ogs_pfcp_xact_local_create() fails)
- Memory shortage (ogs_pkbuf_copy() fails)
- PFCP payload build failure (sgwc_sxa_build_bearer_to_modify_list() fails)
- PFCP transaction update failure (ogs_pfcp_xact_update_tx() fails)

These are all temporary resource issues and should not crash the process.

## Fix

Replace ogs_assert(OGS_OK == ...) with proper error handling:
- Store return value and check for failure
- Log error message for debugging
- Use continue to skip failed session and process remaining sessions

This matches the existing pattern in Release Access Bearers Handler
(same file, lines 1271-1278).

